🐛 Describe the bug
It looks like this:
std::vector<at::Tensor> AOTIModelContainerRunner::run(
    const std::vector<at::Tensor>& inputs,
    AOTInductorStreamHandle cuda_stream_handle) {
  auto input_handles =
      torch::aot_inductor::unsafe_alloc_new_handles_from_tensors(inputs);

  // For outputs, we only allocate a vector to hold returned tensor handles,
  // not allocating the actual output tensor storage here
  size_t num_outputs = 0;
Because it does not steal ownership of inputs, this means inputs must stay live for the entirety of the model run. This can be undesirable for memory usage.
